00:34.840 --> 00:38.300
Ikoku Meiro
no Croisée

00:34.840 --> 00:38.300
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:34.840 --> 00:38.300
Paris. The end of the 19th century.
Beneath the glass ceiling of the Galerie du Roy,
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival...

00:34.840 --> 00:38.300
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:38.300 --> 00:43.680
As I open the gate and step out into the street

00:44.310 --> 00:48.360
asa no hikari ga mabushii

00:44.310 --> 00:48.360
朝の光が眩しい

00:44.310 --> 00:48.360
I can see the sun shining brightly

00:51.360 --> 00:56.360
doko kara ka nagareru hanauta ni

00:51.360 --> 00:56.360
どこからか流れる鼻歌に

00:51.360 --> 00:56.360
I can hear humming in the distance

00:57.530 --> 01:01.290
kokoro hazumi tokete yukuyo

00:57.530 --> 01:01.290
心弾み解けてゆくよ

00:57.530 --> 01:01.290
It moves me and melts my heart

01:04.500 --> 01:09.960
mabuta tojireba ukabu egao

01:04.500 --> 01:09.960
目蓋閉じれば浮かぶ笑顔

01:04.500 --> 01:09.960
I can see that smile when I close my eyes

01:11.130 --> 01:16.550
omoidasu tabi ni namida hitotsu

01:11.130 --> 01:16.550
想い出すたびに涙ひとつ

01:11.130 --> 01:16.550
It brings me to tears whenever I remember it

01:17.050 --> 01:20.180
te wo hiroge hashiridase

01:17.050 --> 01:20.180
手を広げ　走りだせ

01:17.050 --> 01:20.180
Spread your arms out and take off

01:20.180 --> 01:23.520
hi no ataru toori wo

01:20.180 --> 01:23.520
陽のあたる通りを

01:20.180 --> 01:23.520
Down the streets where the lights shine

01:23.520 --> 01:30.060
michiyuku hito ni genki ni aisatsu

01:23.520 --> 01:30.060
道行く人に元気にあいさつ

01:23.520 --> 01:30.060
Cheerfully greet people walking down the city streets

01:30.060 --> 01:36.700
atarashii kimochi de shinkokyuu shitara

01:30.060 --> 01:36.700
新しい 気持ちで　深呼吸したら

01:30.060 --> 01:36.700
Take a deep breath to refresh yourself

01:36.700 --> 01:45.200
kono sekai wa hora itsudemo kimi no mono

01:36.700 --> 01:45.200
この世界はほら、いつでも　君のもの

01:36.700 --> 01:45.200
And this world will always be yours

01:50.630 --> 02:00.590
Episode 08 :

01:50.630 --> 02:00.590
" Kid's Room "

02:20.160 --> 02:22.490
<i>I love you, Claude.</i>

02:23.740 --> 02:25.200
<i>Camille?</i>

02:25.200 --> 02:28.080
<i>I really do love you.</i>

02:28.080 --> 02:33.290
<i>So even if we grow up and I get married,</i>

02:33.290 --> 02:35.170
<i>will you still come over to play?</i>

02:51.480 --> 02:56.610
Stylish kimono are nice, but fancy ones definitely suit you better.

02:57.570 --> 03:02.910
Is it really okay to leave the shopkeeping to you?

03:02.910 --> 03:05.200
She gave you an invitation.

03:05.200 --> 03:09.330
You want Madam Alice to see
that you're feeling better, right?

03:09.330 --> 03:15.670
Yes, she was the one who hired the doctor for me, as well as many other things.

03:15.670 --> 03:19.220
I want to give her my thanks.

03:19.220 --> 03:21.010
That sounds about right.

03:30.100 --> 03:31.060
Wait!

03:31.060 --> 03:33.060
Yune, are you ready to-

03:37.980 --> 03:39.320
I'm sorry.

03:39.940 --> 03:41.400
Claude-sama...

03:42.360 --> 03:45.070
Claude isn't very fond of cats.

03:45.070 --> 03:45.660
What?!

03:45.660 --> 03:47.080
I'm sorry!

03:47.080 --> 03:51.160
No, it's not like I hate the actual cats.

03:51.620 --> 03:53.500
Not the actual cats?

03:55.210 --> 04:01.590
In other words, "All of the cats that I've loved have run away from this house."

04:02.010 --> 04:04.340
You used to have cats here?

04:04.340 --> 04:06.470
Not actual cats.

04:07.220 --> 04:10.180
There's one over at the Blanche household, too.

04:10.180 --> 04:13.060
But that isn't an actual cat, either.

04:13.060 --> 04:15.440
Stop making those metaphors!

04:18.230 --> 04:19.650
Oh, my!

04:19.650 --> 04:21.780
It suits you very well, Onee-sama!

04:23.820 --> 04:28.370
You look more elegant than usual, Onee-sama.

04:28.370 --> 04:32.160
No way! It can't be because Claude Claudel is coming?!

04:32.160 --> 04:34.540
What are you talking about, Alice-chan?

04:34.540 --> 04:37.500
I'm usually right about these kind of things!

04:37.500 --> 04:44.970
Lady Camille will be taking a stroll down Avenue des Champs-Élysées this afternoon with her mother.

04:37.500 --> 04:44.970
This is a large, main street in Paris.

04:44.970 --> 04:46.840
Oh, that's it?

04:47.090 --> 04:51.220
But geez, you're all fancied up in a new hat and dress,

04:51.220 --> 04:54.020
like you're ready to take a stroll in the park on a horse carriage.

04:54.020 --> 04:58.810
You're already out there before you've even debuted into high society!

05:00.190 --> 05:02.940
Just enjoy it as if it were a game.

05:02.940 --> 05:04.490
I could never do that.

05:04.490 --> 05:06.280
I'd be bored to death!

05:06.280 --> 05:12.080
Not to mention it's impossible to find a rich, noble, <i>and</i> kindhearted man.

05:12.080 --> 05:17.210
I wouldn't be able to bear living with a man I don't love,

05:17.210 --> 05:19.750
even if I could have as many <i>amants</i> as I wanted.

05:17.210 --> 05:19.750
An "amant" is an illegitimate male lover.

05:20.500 --> 05:23.380
Marriage should be done for your family's prosperity.

05:23.380 --> 05:26.380
You wouldn't feel angry if you understood that.

05:26.970 --> 05:30.930
Unlike you, nobody expects anything from me, anyway!

05:31.930 --> 05:36.310
Just don't go making <i>that</i> man an <i>amant!</i>

05:36.310 --> 05:39.770
That man is utterly insensitive!

05:39.770 --> 05:45.740
The reason he visited you so frequently in his youth is still a complete mystery to me.

05:45.740 --> 05:48.700
I'll admit that his face and style aren't bad,

05:48.700 --> 05:51.330
but that twisted personality of his...!

05:51.330 --> 05:53.660
He must be your worst enemy.

05:53.660 --> 05:54.950
Excuse me.

05:55.500 --> 05:57.920
Yune-sama and Claude-sama have arrived.

05:58.420 --> 05:59.790
Yune-chan?!

06:03.000 --> 06:05.460
Welcome, Yune-chan!

06:06.010 --> 06:07.760
Welcome to my tea party!

06:09.590 --> 06:12.390
A beautiful kimono as always!

06:12.390 --> 06:16.560
Excuse me for causing you so much trouble, Alice-sama.

06:16.560 --> 06:18.190
It was no problem at all!

06:18.190 --> 06:19.900
You look much better now!

06:19.900 --> 06:21.650
I'm so relieved!

06:22.520 --> 06:25.150
Th-Thank you.

06:25.150 --> 06:26.190
Alice.

06:26.940 --> 06:29.820
You didn't have to follow her here.

06:29.820 --> 06:33.120
Who would protect Yune, then?

06:33.120 --> 06:36.870
I'm surprised you haven't left yet,
considering how many complaints you have.

06:37.620 --> 06:40.250
You did us a favor, after all.

06:41.080 --> 06:43.170
That aside, Yune-chan,

06:43.170 --> 06:43.790
come here!

06:43.790 --> 06:44.420
Huh?

06:44.420 --> 06:45.340
Um-

06:44.630 --> 06:46.420
Come on, this way!

06:45.340 --> 06:47.010
Claude-sama!

06:46.420 --> 06:47.670
Just forget about that guy!

06:47.670 --> 06:48.380
Come on!

06:48.380 --> 06:50.680
I'll wait here, go ahead.

06:55.100 --> 06:58.890
Wouldn't it feel great to have a tea party here?

06:59.940 --> 07:00.890
Yes.

07:00.890 --> 07:06.230
This garden lets you feel the experience of being outdoors, even if you're stuck in this mansion!

07:06.610 --> 07:08.070
That's why I love it!

07:14.070 --> 07:15.740
Monsieur Claudel.

07:16.410 --> 07:18.040
This way, please.

07:18.040 --> 07:19.710
Oh, I-

07:23.420 --> 07:24.670
Camille...

07:29.590 --> 07:32.510
<i>Mother dislikes stray cats.</i>

07:33.340 --> 07:35.260
<i>Even though you have a pet cat?</i>

07:35.260 --> 07:39.560
<i>When they randomly walk into the house as if they belong here,</i>

07:39.560 --> 07:41.890
<i>it reminds her of a prostitute or </i>amant.<i></i>

07:42.270 --> 07:46.400
<i>That's why she never lets her cat leave the room.</i>

07:46.400 --> 07:48.440
<i>Poor cat...</i>

07:55.700 --> 07:58.120
<i>I like stray cats more!</i>

08:04.960 --> 08:06.920
Please, have a seat.

08:09.130 --> 08:11.300
You look like a cowardly mouse.

08:17.180 --> 08:20.100
Was that a bit rude of me?

08:25.980 --> 08:27.980
It brings back memories, doesn't it?

08:28.360 --> 08:34.530
I was always so excited when you'd bring stray cats over.

08:37.030 --> 08:40.540
Yune-chan is just like me when I was younger.

08:40.540 --> 08:43.000
Yune is nothing like you.

08:43.000 --> 08:44.620
She's become a rumor, you know?

08:45.330 --> 08:50.000
She's always at your side, looking up to you.

08:51.130 --> 08:53.550
No matter what country they are born in,

08:53.550 --> 08:55.760
girls will be girls.

08:55.760 --> 08:57.930
You sound like you know everything.

08:57.930 --> 09:00.430
You're the one who doesn't know.

09:01.350 --> 09:04.890
Something much more significant than nationality.

09:05.600 --> 09:08.520
Something that we're born with.

09:10.110 --> 09:13.240
How old is she?

09:14.030 --> 09:16.070
Why did she come all the way here?

09:16.070 --> 09:17.990
What's her family's status?

09:17.990 --> 09:19.990
What kind of education did she receive?

09:21.410 --> 09:22.620
You don't know?

09:23.830 --> 09:26.620
It doesn't matter to me.

09:29.170 --> 09:30.880
You trust her, don't you?

09:35.010 --> 09:38.590
I only came because you did us a favor.

09:38.590 --> 09:41.050
I don't really want to be here.

09:41.050 --> 09:43.180
Yune's being manipulated by Alice,

09:43.180 --> 09:44.980
just like a doll would be.

09:44.980 --> 09:48.650
Is that something that you should be saying?

09:50.060 --> 09:53.400
I like that part of you...

09:53.400 --> 09:55.190
but it's a bit cruel.

10:13.550 --> 10:15.920
A fairy tale?

10:15.920 --> 10:16.920
Yes!

10:16.920 --> 10:19.340
Japan has them too, right?

10:19.340 --> 10:22.890
They have many mysterious occurrences, after all!

10:22.890 --> 10:26.180
There must be many interesting stories!

10:26.180 --> 10:27.940
Fairy tales...

10:33.820 --> 10:36.570
There's a story called Momotaro.

10:36.570 --> 10:37.950
Momotaro?

10:37.950 --> 10:39.150
Yes!

10:39.150 --> 10:41.450
Momotaro, a boy born from within a peach,

10:41.450 --> 10:45.910
defeats demons with a dog, monkey, and pheasant!

10:45.910 --> 10:49.160
A peach, a dog, monkey, and pheasant...?

10:49.790 --> 10:52.540
Let's go defeat demons!

10:52.540 --> 10:53.630
Something like this?

10:54.130 --> 10:56.170
No, not quite.

10:56.170 --> 10:59.800
He was born from a peach, but he is a normal human.

11:00.260 --> 11:02.510
A human was born?

11:04.640 --> 11:07.140
How cute!

11:08.560 --> 11:11.940
It's not just any peach, but a giant peach, so...

11:11.940 --> 11:16.070
Oh, how about Saru Kani Gassen?

11:11.940 --> 11:16.070
You can look this stuff up if you want to know more.

11:16.360 --> 11:17.480
Sarukani?

11:17.480 --> 11:20.400
Yes, the crab had an onigiri-

11:20.400 --> 11:21.740
Onigiri?

11:21.740 --> 11:26.120
Onigiri are balls of steamed rice.

11:26.120 --> 11:27.620
Why is it a ball?

11:27.620 --> 11:29.080
Um...

11:29.080 --> 11:33.920
You can eat it without chopsticks,
and it's easy to carry around.

11:33.920 --> 11:35.500
Amazing!

11:35.500 --> 11:38.550
That's part of Japan's wisdom!

11:38.550 --> 11:39.550
Yes!

11:41.430 --> 11:42.470
Go on.

11:42.470 --> 11:44.800
R-Right...

11:49.600 --> 11:52.100
Oh, you're keeping shop?

11:52.100 --> 11:52.980
Where's Claude?

11:53.400 --> 11:55.900
He went to meet with a cat.

11:55.900 --> 11:56.980
A cat?

11:56.980 --> 11:58.690
It's good for him.

12:01.280 --> 12:03.200
I even got him a nice bottle.

12:03.200 --> 12:04.450
What do you say?

12:04.450 --> 12:05.950
Sounds great!

12:05.950 --> 12:09.040
I was just about ready to get out of here.

12:10.080 --> 12:11.660
Let's keep this a secret from Claude.

12:11.660 --> 12:13.830
Whatever!

12:23.340 --> 12:27.640
Princess Kaguya gave the men impossible demands,

12:27.640 --> 12:30.020
and declined all of their marriage offers.

12:30.020 --> 12:34.480
Even so, there were countless men who admired Princess Kaguya.

12:34.480 --> 12:36.360
Then, on the night of a full moon,

12:36.360 --> 12:38.690
several men were sent down from the moon,

12:38.690 --> 12:44.150
and the princess left the potion of immortality to her beloved emperor.

12:44.400 --> 12:54.580
However, the emperor burned the potion because he did not want to live forever without Princess Kaguya.

12:56.380 --> 13:00.840
Women are allowed to choose their lovers?!

13:00.840 --> 13:02.420
Japan must be so advanced!

13:03.970 --> 13:09.350
In French tales, women cannot awake from eternal sleep without a prince's kiss,

13:09.350 --> 13:12.770
or become a queen unless her foot fits a glass slipper!

13:12.770 --> 13:14.600
It's a disgrace to women!

13:14.600 --> 13:16.310
I-I suppose.

13:20.360 --> 13:24.570
I think I understand how we're alike now.

13:25.110 --> 13:27.200
We are?

13:27.200 --> 13:30.410
Japanese women must be strong.

13:30.410 --> 13:34.200
One came all the way to Paris, after all!

13:34.200 --> 13:36.290
That's very significant!

13:37.370 --> 13:39.790
Y-You think so?

13:40.380 --> 13:41.420
Yes!

13:45.050 --> 13:48.590
I'll let you hear my stories, now!

13:48.590 --> 13:50.100
Come on, Yune-chan!

13:50.100 --> 13:52.310
Yes, Alice-sama!

14:06.400 --> 14:09.610
This used to be the kid's room for Onee-sama and I.

14:09.610 --> 14:12.240
Nothing's changed.

14:12.240 --> 14:13.950
Look!

14:15.540 --> 14:18.080
I drew that when I was ten.

14:18.830 --> 14:20.710
You did?

14:20.710 --> 14:22.380
It's an Eastern dragon.

14:23.590 --> 14:28.720
My story was about a girl who lived far, far away.

14:29.720 --> 14:35.430
<i>The young girl, who crossed many oceans to come to this far away land,</i>

14:35.430 --> 14:39.020
<i>met another girl in that foreign land.</i>

14:39.310 --> 14:44.270
<i>That girl had eyes the color of the sea, and hair the color of the golden sun.</i>

14:44.270 --> 14:51.030
<i>The young girl, on the other hand, had eyes and hair as black as night.</i>

14:51.030 --> 14:57.160
<i>However, that blackness was striking to the other girl,</i>

14:57.160 --> 15:01.080
<i>and she fell in love with her!</i>

15:01.080 --> 15:03.960
<i>The two talked about what they liked,</i>

15:03.960 --> 15:06.000
<i>taught each other dances,</i>

15:06.000 --> 15:08.800
<i>and became friends in no time!</i>

15:08.800 --> 15:12.050
<i>"What's on the other side of the ocean?"</i>

15:12.050 --> 15:15.060
<i>the black-eyed girl asked.</i>

15:18.020 --> 15:20.940
<i>What did the blue-eyed girl say?</i>

15:21.850 --> 15:23.690
<i>She said,</i>

15:27.530 --> 15:33.320
<i>"I don't know, because the world beyond the ocean is endless,</i>

15:33.320 --> 15:36.740
<i>and has many things that I don't know about!"</i>

15:38.750 --> 15:40.960
<i>But then she said,</i>

15:40.960 --> 15:43.920
<i>"Why don't we go explore it on a dragon?</i>

15:43.920 --> 15:47.590
<i>We could freely explore the starry skies that way!"</i>

15:48.800 --> 15:52.930
<i>Hearing that, the girl's black eyes began to shine with joy!</i>

15:52.930 --> 15:54.050
<i>Wonderful!</i>

15:54.050 --> 15:55.390
<i>A dragon tour!</i>

15:55.390 --> 15:58.100
<i>You're invited, of course!</i>

15:58.100 --> 15:59.270
<i>Really?!</i>

15:59.270 --> 16:01.520
<i>Yes! Let's go together!</i>

16:04.520 --> 16:10.780
<i>And so, the two went on the dragon and flew up into the sky!</i>

16:24.960 --> 16:27.290
That was my story.

16:28.460 --> 16:30.880
Wouldn't it be nice if we could do that?

16:30.880 --> 16:34.720
I would take you, Onee-sama, and people whom I love.

16:36.260 --> 16:37.430
I know!

16:37.430 --> 16:39.430
I have an idea!

16:39.430 --> 16:42.180
Wait right here, Yune-chan!

16:44.980 --> 16:47.230
I'll give you a surprise!

16:47.230 --> 16:49.320
A-Alice-sama!

16:56.200 --> 16:57.570
What a troublemaker.

16:58.780 --> 17:00.790
She left her guest all alone.

17:00.790 --> 17:02.330
Camille-sama!

17:02.330 --> 17:05.170
Alice-chan acts on whim.

17:05.710 --> 17:11.090
That freedom is her specialty, though.

17:12.960 --> 17:14.260
Yes.

17:17.390 --> 17:18.800
Um-

17:18.800 --> 17:19.640
Yes?

17:20.600 --> 17:23.270
No, it's nothing.

17:24.480 --> 17:26.600
If you have something to say, say it.

17:26.600 --> 17:29.020
I'm sorry.

17:30.230 --> 17:37.030
I had an older sister at home
who was very kind, just like you.

17:37.910 --> 17:41.530
I don't intend on making you my younger sister.

17:41.530 --> 17:44.500
What reminded you of her?

17:45.540 --> 17:47.040
I'm sorry.

17:47.330 --> 17:50.420
You admit your blunder when you apologize.

17:51.130 --> 17:55.130
You're simply calling yourself an idiot.

17:55.920 --> 17:58.430
Stop smiling at everyone you see, too.

17:59.930 --> 18:01.050
Okay...

18:03.010 --> 18:04.430
Come over here.

18:09.060 --> 18:13.610
These clothes are all from when we were younger.

18:13.610 --> 18:15.570
Do you want to try any of them on?

18:16.860 --> 18:20.240
Go on, you can choose whichever you like.

18:39.050 --> 18:40.180
This...

18:46.220 --> 18:48.180
That's a good choice.

18:48.180 --> 18:49.940
What caught your eye?

18:49.940 --> 18:56.820
Claude-sama once told me that frilly sleeves were a nuisance, so...

18:57.320 --> 19:00.820
I chose one with less decorations on the sleeves.

19:01.490 --> 19:06.790
Claude wouldn't praise you for choosing things based on his opinion.

19:08.410 --> 19:11.250
No matter how much thought you put into a dress or decorations,

19:12.040 --> 19:14.500
he won't see any part of it.

19:15.090 --> 19:18.590
Even if he does, it would just be-

19:19.470 --> 19:20.800
What's so funny?

19:22.140 --> 19:24.720
No, um...

19:24.720 --> 19:25.970
I...

19:26.720 --> 19:28.640
I think so, too!

19:32.650 --> 19:38.400
I was happy that I could talk so much about Claude-sama.

19:38.400 --> 19:39.780
I'm sorry.

19:39.780 --> 19:42.860
I'm sorr- I mean-

19:42.860 --> 19:45.370
Uh- Um...

19:46.660 --> 19:48.080
Try it on.

19:50.750 --> 19:52.330
I'll help you.

19:53.630 --> 19:54.580
Thank you!

19:56.290 --> 20:01.470
Girls need to understand their strong points,

20:01.470 --> 20:04.930
and find something that suits them best.

20:04.930 --> 20:08.850
You'll be made fun of in Paris if you can't do that.

20:09.390 --> 20:10.230
Okay.

20:11.020 --> 20:13.440
Thank you.

20:13.440 --> 20:17.440
This room holds many of my happiest memories.

20:18.110 --> 20:25.030
I had a nanny when I was little, and always studied here unless I was eating,

20:25.030 --> 20:29.080
but Alice-chan often got scolded for sneaking out.

20:29.330 --> 20:32.500
The marks on the chair are from the ropes that Alice-chan tied onto it.

20:33.620 --> 20:38.380
She stacked up chairs so she could draw on the ceiling.

20:39.130 --> 20:41.090
<i>That's dangerous, Alice-chan!</i>

20:41.090 --> 20:42.380
<i>Alice-chan!</i>

20:42.380 --> 20:44.260
<i>Look, Onee-sama!</i>

20:44.260 --> 20:45.640
<i>It's an Eastern dragon!</i>

20:46.010 --> 20:50.270
<i>It can fly anywhere, and it's going to go on a trip through the night sky!</i>

20:50.270 --> 20:52.060
<i>You're going, too!</i>

20:55.940 --> 21:02.490
Alice-chan was wearing that dress when she told the story of the dragon.

21:03.820 --> 21:11.080
It was also a dress given to a foreign girl who she could talk on and on with...

21:13.080 --> 21:14.250
Take it.

21:17.580 --> 21:26.260
sukitooru hitomi ga sagasu takaramono wa

21:17.580 --> 21:26.260
透き通る瞳が  探す宝物は

21:17.580 --> 21:26.260
Your crystal clear eyes were looking for a treasure

21:20.500 --> 21:21.590
But...

21:23.420 --> 21:27.680
This place is probably too cramped for Alice-chan,

21:27.590 --> 21:35.310
doko ni aru no kana to kokoro odoraseta

21:27.590 --> 21:35.310
どこにあるのかなと  心踊らせた

21:27.590 --> 21:35.310
My heart danced, wondering where it might be

21:27.680 --> 21:32.640
so I want you to tell her stories
from the other side of the world.

21:33.770 --> 21:34.600
I will.

21:37.350 --> 21:46.360
waraigoe ga hibiku hikari no madogiwa de

21:37.350 --> 21:46.360
笑い声が響く  光の窓際で

21:37.350 --> 21:46.360
As laughter rang out through the bright window

21:47.200 --> 21:54.830
hirogaru aozora ni asu wo egaiteta

21:47.200 --> 21:54.830
広がる青空に  明日を描いてた

21:47.200 --> 21:54.830
I painted tomorrow onto the endless blue sky

22:01.000 --> 22:05.720
kyou no kimi no yoin de

22:01.000 --> 22:05.720
今日の君の余韻で

22:01.000 --> 22:05.720
Your afterglow today

22:06.170 --> 22:20.150
kotoba ni dekinai ondo ni tsutsumareta

22:06.170 --> 22:20.150
言葉に出来ない温度に包まれた

22:06.170 --> 22:20.150
Enclosed me in an indescribable warmth

22:20.650 --> 22:30.620
dakara warattari naitari butsukatte mitari

22:20.650 --> 22:30.620
だから笑ったり泣いたりぶつかってみたり

22:20.650 --> 22:30.620
So I can smile, cry, and be a little bold

22:21.560 --> 22:23.900
Something's missing...

22:25.110 --> 22:29.410
Bring some Japanese chochin and umbrellas from my room!

22:29.410 --> 22:30.870
Yes, Ma'am.

22:30.620 --> 22:40.330
kazaranai watashi no mama sunao de irareru

22:30.620 --> 22:40.330
飾らない私のまま  素直でいられる

22:30.620 --> 22:40.330
Staying simple and true to myself

22:30.870 --> 22:33.990
Hurry! I don't want to bore Yune-chan to death!

22:33.990 --> 22:34.950
Yes, Ma'am.

22:40.460 --> 22:50.090
itsumo yasashiku egao de kimi wo mitsumetara

22:40.460 --> 22:50.090
いつも優しく笑顔で  君を見つめたら

22:40.460 --> 22:50.090
Always watching you with a kind smile

22:50.470 --> 23:01.020
asu wa motto yawaraka na ichinichi ni naru deshou

22:50.470 --> 23:01.020
明日はもっと柔らかな  一日になるでしょう

22:50.470 --> 23:01.020
I know tomorrow will be an even more tender day

23:34.640 --> 23:35.720
Next Episode:

23:34.850 --> 23:40.480
Episode 09 :

23:35.720 --> 23:36.930
Secret.

23:36.930 --> 23:38.470
Please watch it.
